  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 6-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate. Stack sequence: Air | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Si(semi-infinite). Initialize thicknesses from prior best candidate [44.96, 138.94, 161.65, 243.43, 124.89, 37.78] nm. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with exploration radius ±10 nm per layer. Evaluate unpolarized reflectance and transmittance at 0 deg incidence over 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm bands. Thickness bounds: 20-400 nm per layer. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
